  "question": {
    "text": "A thin plano convex lens made of glass of refractive index 1.5 is immersed in a liquid of refractive index 1.2. When the plane side of the lens is silver coated for complete reflection, the lens immersed in the liquid behaves like a concave mirror of focal length 0.2 m . The radius of curvature of the curved surface of the lens is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "0.20 m",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0.25 m",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0.15 m",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0.10 m",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0051_adfe8ecb270f.png\"><br>\n\n\n\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1.5}{\\mathrm{v}}=\\frac{1.5-1.2}{\\mathrm{R}} \\\\ & \\mathrm{v}=\\frac{1.5 \\mathrm{R}}{0.3}=5 \\mathrm{R} \\\\ & \\frac{1.2}{\\mathrm{f}}-\\frac{1.5}{5 \\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{1.2-1.5}{-\\mathrm{R}} \\\\ & \\frac{1.2}{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{0.3}{\\mathrm{R}} \\times 2 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{f}=2 \\mathrm{R} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{R}=0.1\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}